            "description": "Watch Independiente del Valle vs Rosario Central highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 27, 2026. The stage was set for a classic CONMEBOL Libertadores encounter as Independiente del Valle hosted Rosario Central in a match of high stakes. Both teams aimed to assert their dominance in a fixture where tactical discipline was expected to be the deciding factor. A Gritty Opening Period Played on May 27, 2026 , the match began with a display of physical football that set the tone for the evening. Rosario Central were the first to feel the referee's scrutiny when Enzo Copetti was shown a yellow card in the 13th minute for a robust challenge. The first half remained a cagey affair, with both midfields battling fiercely for possession and clear-cut chances remaining at a premium. As the clock ticked towards the break, tensions boiled over in stoppage time. A heated exchange resulted in yellow cards for both Independiente del Valle 's Junior Sornoza and Rosario Central 's star man Angel Di Maria . The stalemate at halftime was a fair reflection of a period where defensive solidity outweighed attacking flair. The Breakthrough from the Spot The deadlock was finally broken in the 64th minute of the second half. Independiente del Valle were awarded a penalty, and it was their talisman Junior Sornoza who stepped up to the spot. With clinical precision, he sent the ball past the goalkeeper to make it 1-0, giving the home side a lead they had fought hard to earn. Rosario Central attempted to claw their way back, but their frustration grew as the minutes passed. Guillermo Fernandez received a yellow card shortly after the goal as the visitors struggled to find their rhythm. Managerial changes followed for both sides, with the Argentine club introducing veteran Marco Ruben in hopes of an equalizer, while the hosts brought on fresh legs to protect their narrow advantage. Holding Firm Under Pressure The final stages of the match saw a flurry of substitutions as Independiente del Valle looked to see out the game. Youri Ochoa and Steven Gongora were introduced late on to provide defensive cover. Despite Rosario Central 's late efforts and a final yellow card for Ignacio Ovando in injury time, the home side held firm to secure a vital victory and three precious points in their continental campaign.",
